  "published": "2026-03-04T14:18:14.437Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixed:\n- ProjectionManager.UpdateAsync correctness bug — duplicate event application and checkpoint regression resolved. Events are now filtered by both event type and position inside the per-projection lock; checkpoint always advances to batchMax.\n- RebuildAsync / RebuildAllAsync — checkpoint file is now always written after a rebuild, even when the event store is empty. Prevents infinite re-queue on daemon restart.\n\nRemoved:\n- Sample: CourseBookOrderHistory projection removed. It used evt.Position as key selector (O(Events) cardinality), producing 700,000+ files on a Large-seeded database. Covered by the correctly-designed StudentPurchasedBooks projection (O(Students)).\n\nPerformance (2026-03-03):\n- Incremental projection update: 3.68 us / 0 B (zero-allocation hot path verified).\n- ReadLastAsync: 799 us (100 events) to 1,105 us (10,000 events) — near-O(1) confirmed.\n- High-selectivity tag query: 553 us to ~501 us (-9%).\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/majormartintibor/Opossum/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
